    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Call Of Home is Held By Trees’ third studio album, expanding the British project’s atmospheric rock and post-rock vocabulary beyond its Talk Talk-influenced beginnings. The roughly hour-long set balances spacious, carefully layered instrumentals with a more song-oriented approach, pairing reflective arrangements with an emotional focus on belonging, memory, movement, and home.\n\nNine vocal tracks are framed by the instrumental pieces “In This Moment” and “The Sound Of Home,” while guest appearances broaden the album’s palette: Simone Marie, Jason Upton, Martin Smith, Eric Bibb, and Marc James each contribute distinctive voices. “Needed Time” brings Bibb’s blues sensibility into the group’s expansive sound, and “Belong” adds a more driving, guitar-led intensity. Released by Tweed Jacket Music Ltd., the album represents a notable evolution for Held By Trees—warmer, more varied, and more direct while retaining the patient atmospherics and musicianship associated with the band.",
